<title>EGYPT: Egypt yr-on-yr inflation down to 5.4 pct in April.</title>
<headline>Egypt yr-on-yr inflation down to 5.4 pct in April.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian year-on-year inflation fell to 5.4 percent in April, from 5.5 percent in March and 7.4 percent in April 1996, officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The consumer price index for urban areas, set at a base of 100 in the financial year 1986/7, rose 0.6 percent in April, to 381.0 from 378.7 in March 1997, they said. The index stood at 361.6 at the end of April 1996.</p>
<p>				    April 1997  March 1997  April 1996</p>
<p>    Month-on-month		 +0.6	  +0.6	  +0.8</p>
<p>    Year-on-year		   +5.4	  +5.5	  +7.4</p>
<p>    INDEX (base 1986/7)	 381.0	 378.7	 361.6</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Wright +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
